1532 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 234 0 R
/T (The application was demonstrated using a small set of meaningful sample records spanning all six waste categories, a mix of recycled and non-recycled entries, several different dates within a two-week window, and a realistic range of weights \(roughly 0.7 kg to 3.2 kg per entry\). This was enough sample data to produce non-trivial totals, a clear hotspot, and a recycling rate meaningfully below 100%, so that every analysis and recommendation feature could be demonstrated with genuine output rather than placeholder values.)
/E (The application was demonstrated using a small set of meaningful sample records spanning all six waste categories, a mix of recycled and non-recycled entries, several different dates within a two-week window, and a realistic range of weights \(roughly 0.7 kg to 3.2 kg per entry\). This was enough sample data to produce non-trivial totals, a clear hotspot, and a recycling rate meaningfully below 100%, so that every analysis and recommendation feature could be demonstrated with genuine output rather than placeholder values.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
