3403 0 obj
<<
/Title (TerraLoop was validated through manual functional testing using meaningful, hand-entered sample data covering all six categories, a mix of recycled and non-recycled entries, and a range of dates and weights. Each core feature was exercised directly through the interface and checked against the expected result. No automated unit-test suite has been built for this prototype; testing to date has been manual and feature-by-feature.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3228 0 R
/Next 3484 0 R
>>
endobj
3404 0 obj
<<
/Title (Expected Result)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3228 0 R
/Prev 3485 0 R
/First 3486 0 R
/Last 3487 0 R
/Count -14
>>
endobj
3405 0 obj
<<
/Title (The application was demonstrated using a small set of meaningful sample records spanning all six waste categories, a mix of recycled and non-recycled entries, several different dates within a two-week window, and a realistic range of weights \(roughly 0.7 kg to 3.2 kg per entry\). This was enough sample data to produce non-trivial totals, a clear hotspot, and a recycling rate meaningfully below 100%, so that every analysis and recommendation feature could be demonstrated with genuine output rather than placeholder values.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3229 0 R
>>
endobj
